  "headline": "MPR Discusses Election Mechanism For New Vice President Nominees",
  "seoTitle": "MPR Discusses Vice President Election Date",
  "metaDescription": "The MPR is drafting the election and inauguration mechanisms for the new Vice President, while debating the scheduling of the parliamentary session.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The MPR Ad Hoc Committee is drafting regulations for the election and inauguration of the new Vice President for the 2024-2029 term.",
    "Proposals include a 14-day working interval after the President submits candidate names, with potential scenarios for tie-breaking votes.",
    "Concerns have been raised regarding the feasibility of the December 9, 2026, session date given the timeline for candidate submission."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) of Indonesia is actively working on the legislative framework to fill the vacant Vice Presidential seat for the remainder of the 2024-2029 term. Following the vacancy, the MPR established an Ad Hoc Committee tasked with defining the voting procedures, including how to handle potential deadlocks. Discussions are currently focused on the formal mechanics of the election and the official inauguration date. While there has been discussion about holding a plenary session on December 9, 2026, public and political figures, including Mahfud MD, have noted that the timeline depends on when President Prabowo Subianto submits the two required candidate names. The committee is balancing the need for a swift selection process with the legal requirements for a transparent and structured election procedure as the nation anticipates the upcoming nomination process.",
